## 8. Google-Assistant-like reference architecture mapped to A.I.R.A.

The reference model is a pipeline, not a single LLM:

```text
Wake word
    ↓
Audio processing
    ↓
ASR (speech → text)
    ↓
NLU (what does the user mean?)
    ↓
Dialog manager / agent orchestration
    ↓
Context & state / memory
    ↓
Search, APIs, apps, coding agent, automation
    ↓
Response generation
    ↓
TTS (text → speech)
    ↓
Device / OS layer
```

Mapping to A.I.R.A.:

| Reference layer | A.I.R.A. equivalent | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Wake-word detection | Future voice interface | ⏳ |
| Audio processing | Future voice layer | ⏳ |
| ASR | Speech-to-text input | ⏳ |
| NLU | Intent and task understanding | ⏳ |
| Dialog manager | Agent orchestration and planner | ⏳ |
| Context and state | **Current memory system** | 🔄 |
| Search / APIs / apps | Research engine, tools, OS integrations | ✅ / ⏳ |
| Response generation | LLM and response layer | ✅ |
| TTS | Future voice output | ⏳ |
| Device layer | Future computer, OS, and IoT control | ⏳ |

The current work belongs primarily to **Context & State → Memory**:

```text
extractor
    ↓
validator
    ↓
memory_db
    ↓
retriever
    ↓
LLM context
```

This reference architecture should guide future design without being treated as A.I.R.A.’s final architecture. Layers may later be combined, split, or expanded.

